---
import CTA from './CTA.astro';
import InsightRow from './InsightCard.astro';
import articles from '../data/articles.json';
import portfolio from '../data/portfolio.json';
import fdf from '../data/fdf.json';
import apis from '../data/apis.json';
const featured = [...articles].sort((a,b) => new Date(b.date).getTime()-new Date(a.date).getTime()).slice(0,3);
const fmt = (n:number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
const entries = [
  { href:'/fdf', name:'Finished dosage forms', text:`${portfolio.counts.total} hospital and specialty medicines, and a reference list of ${fmt(fdf.length)} products.` },
  { href:'/api', name:'Active pharmaceutical ingredients', text:`A reference range of ${fmt(apis.length)} substances for sourcing enquiries.` },
  { href:'/excipient', name:'Excipients', text:'Formulation materials, requested by grade and specification.' },
  { href:'/nutrition', name:'Nutrition ingredients', text:'Vitamins and nutrition ingredients, with their own reference database.' },
];
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container hero-main">
    <h1>Medicines and pharmaceutical ingredients for Iran, sourced and registered by one team.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Hanpars imports active ingredients, finished medicines, excipients and nutrition ingredients, and prepares their registration with the Iranian authority. We work from Tehran with manufacturers in Türkiye, China, India and Europe, and with the hospitals, distributors and project teams who use what we bring in.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/contact-us-1?type=sourcing">Prepare a sourcing enquiry</a><a class="text-link" href="/regulatory-affairs">Talk to the regulatory team</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-meta"><div class="container hero-meta-inner">{entries.map(entry => <a href={entry.href}><strong>{entry.name}</strong><span>{entry.text}</span></a>)}</div></div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Three things we do, usually together.</h2><p class="lede">A supply agreement is only useful once the product is approved and on the shelf. So sourcing, registration and project coordination sit with the same people.</p></div>
    <div class="columns-3">
      <article class="column-item"><h3>Import and sourcing</h3><p>We find the substance or finished product you need from manufacturers we already work with, and bring it into Iran with the documents the authority will ask for: certificates of analysis, GMP evidence and stability data, agreed before the first order rather than chased afterwards.</p><a class="text-link" href="/api">Browse the API reference range</a></article>
      <article class="column-item"><h3>Regulatory affairs</h3><p>Dossiers in CTD, eCTD or ACTD format, submission to the IFDA and to TİTCK in Türkiye, correspondence with the authority, and keeping the authorisation current after approval. Offered on its own, or alongside the products we supply.</p><a class="text-link" href="/regulatory-affairs">What the regulatory team covers</a></article>
      <article class="column-item"><h3>Development partnerships</h3><p>For finished dosage-form projects we coordinate development and manufacturing partners: formulation, analytical work, scale-up, stability and technology transfer, with each party's responsibilities written down at the start. Hanpars does not own the plants; we run the project.</p><a class="text-link" href="/fdf-cdmo">How a CDMO project begins</a></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-navy">
  <div class="container spotlight">
    <div>
      <h2>The hospital and specialty portfolio</h2>
      <div class="spotlight-figure"><div><strong class="num">{portfolio.counts.total}</strong><span>medicines registered with the IFDA</span></div><div><strong class="num">{portfolio.counts.available}</strong><span>available in Iran today</span></div><div><strong class="num">{portfolio.counts.launching}</strong><span>launching</span></div></div>
      <p>Contrast media, anaesthetics, antibiotics, hormones, biologics: medicines that hospitals cannot run out of, imported from GMP-certified manufacturers in Türkiye, China and India and distributed nationally through Pakhsh Razi, Darougostar Tooba and Dey Darou Omid. Hanpars is also a contracted supplier to the national Strategic Medicine Reserve.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/fdf#product-portfolio">See the full portfolio</a><a class="text-link" href="/contact-us-1?type=regulatory">Represent your products in Iran</a></div>
      <p class="spotlight-note">Status as of {portfolio.snapshot}. Dosage forms and strengths as licensed by the IFDA; confirm current availability when you enquire.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="area-list">{portfolio.groups.map(group => <li><a href={`/fdf#portfolio-${group.id}`}>{group.title}<small>{group.products.length} {group.products.length === 1 ? 'medicine' : 'medicines'}</small></a></li>)}</ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-paper">
  <div class="container company-note">
    <div>
      <span class="persian-name" lang="fa">شرکت هانیا پرسان دارو</span>
      <address class="address">Haniya Parsan Darou Co.<br/>3rd floor, No. 326, Zafar Street<br/>Africa Boulevard, Tehran<small>Office hours 09:00–17:00 ·<a href="tel:+982188856347">+98 21 8885 6347</a></small></address>
      <a class="text-link" href="/about-us">About Hanpars</a>
    </div>
    <div class="copy">
      <p>Hanpars is a pharmaceutical trading company in Tehran. We are the marketing authorisation holder for the medicines we import, which means the dossier, the IRC licence and pharmacovigilance are handled by us, not passed along. It also means that when a hospital pharmacist or a distributor calls about a product, the person who answers knows its file.</p>
      <p>We describe our role precisely. We source, register and coordinate; manufacturers manufacture, and the authority decides. A clear brief at the beginning, and clear responsibilities throughout, is how we keep projects moving.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/culture">How we work</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>How a request proceeds</h2><p class="lede">You do not need a finished specification to start. A product name and a destination are enough for a first conversation.</p></div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step"><h3>Tell us what you need</h3><p>The molecule or product, the strength or grade if you know it, the quantity, and where it is going. For a regulatory or CDMO question: the product and the stage you have reached.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><h3>We put it in context</h3><p>Which manufacturers can supply it, what the target market will require in documents and studies, and what is realistic for timing. We come back with questions before we come back with promises.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><h3>We agree the scope</h3><p>Who does what, in writing: sourcing, dossier, submission, import, distribution. Then the work starts, with one contact at Hanpars accountable for it.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-paper section-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>From the archive</h2><a class="text-link" href="/blog-1">All archived articles</a></div>
    <ul class="insight-list">{featured.map(article => <li><InsightRow article={article}/></li>)}</ul>
    <p class="reference-note">Dated editorial commentary, kept with its original publication dates. It is not a current market forecast or regulatory advice.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<CTA />
